body:
Policy was good value for the protection it provided and peace of mind;
Policy was easy to set up;
Luckily didn't have to use it.

Here is what 1Cover's travel alert and news says about Coronavirus:

Policy coverage position

Our policies contain exclusions relating to an epidemic or pandemic and also known events in the mass media.

Therefore, regardless of when you purchased your policy and the destination:

- It is unlikely that any claim will be covered if it relates to the Coronavirus;
- This applies to all countries, including countries where DFAT has not yet issued a Coronavirus (COVID-19) travel-related warning;
- However, we will assess each claim based on its individual facts and circumstances and policy terms and conditions;

I bought annual multi travel policy last July and it is now worth less than the pdf file that contains the policy (given the situation).

Because of this exclusion, people are less likely to travel.  Therefore, 1Cover can happily enjoy their free ride.

Make sure you understand their fine prints before giving them your hard earn money.

Very happy how to claim dealt with quick as well. This was a breath of fresh air after dealing with AIR NZ who handle my claim terribly.
) 
;) ;)

Chosen because:  as a Senior I had a 15% discount;  
the customer service was VERY good -  helpful, not at all condescending, addressed my individual needs, provided thorough advice and assistance enabling me to make an informed decision;
easy to access on line BUT
....Once I had a quote over the phone I was unable to access that quote on line as the on line application would not recognise my quote number.  Annoying that I had to ring three times before I was able to purchase the Insurance.

We have used InsureandGo on 6 occasions now;
Good value and easy to setup especially as we now purchase annual/multi coverage;
When we made a claim on a previous policy it was dealt with professionally and was quickly resolved.
